<title><![CDATA[Plan to turn Hong Kong office block into flats rejected amid high commercial vacancy rates]]></title>
<link>https://www.scmp.com/business/china-business/article/3369122/plan-turn-hong-kong-office-block-flats-rejected-amid-high-commercial-vacancy-rates</link>
<guid isPermaLink="true">https://www.scmp.com/business/china-business/article/3369122/plan-turn-hong-kong-office-block-flats-rejected-amid-high-commercial-vacancy-rates</guid>
<description><![CDATA[The Town Planning Board turned down a proposal to convert a 1980s office tower in Wan Chai into 180 flats, saying the city still needs Grade B office space even as vacancies hover near 17 per cent. Developers had hoped the case would pave the way for more conversions.]]></description>
